WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.927
This episode focuses on public-sector statistics.

2
00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:10.752
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:10.752 --> 00:00:18.446
The Annual Survey of State and Local Government Finances provides nationwide statistics on revenue, expenditure, debt, and assets.

4
00:00:18.446 --> 00:00:24.424
The Census of Governments supplies a broader recurring census of public organizations and activities.

5
00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:32.975
Census government-finance categories support comparison across jurisdictions, but they do not mirror every line in a city's audited statements.

6
00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:38.536
Functional classifications, fiscal years, government coverage, and revisions must be checked.

7
00:00:38.536 --> 00:00:45.900
Use federal statistics for consistent benchmarking and local audited reports for the City's authoritative financial presentation.

8
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:52.293
Reconcile definitions before explaining a difference rather than choosing whichever figure seems more favorable.

9
00:00:52.293 --> 00:00:53.878
Torrance application segment.

10
00:00:53.878 --> 00:00:57.757
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

11
00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:07.209
The cited City of Torrance primary source is Audit Reports, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/Departments-Offices/Departments-Offices/Finance/Audit-Reports.

12
00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:17.044
For a local analysis, cite Torrance's Annual Comprehensive Financial Report for local audited figures and Census government-finance data for separately labeled national comparison.

13
00:01:17.044 --> 00:01:24.748
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

14
00:01:24.748 --> 00:01:34.525
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

15
00:01:34.525 --> 00:01:37.704
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

16
00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:42.383
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

17
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:46.582
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

18
00:01:46.582 --> 00:01:52.460
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

19
00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.719
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
